From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] zram: use the lzo compressor instead of lz4

The 3.10 tree ships the original 2013 LG LZ4 import (lib/lz4, "Based on LZ4
implementation by Yann Collet, Copyright 2011-2012"), the version upstream
replaced wholesale in 4.11 for correctness. Under heavy zram swap it can
return corrupt bytes on swap-in, seen as cross-process memory corruption:
an ART region-space GC abort (com.android.vending,
region_space_alloc_size=1364202384), a SIGSEGV executing a non-executable
page (com.spotify.music), and downloaded Play Store APK bytes failing their
own signature. The kernel default compressor is lzo; this rc overrode it to
lz4. Use lzo, the long-proven default, and keep zram enabled.

---
 ramdisk/etc/init.samsungexynos7420.rc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ramdisk/etc/init.samsungexynos7420.rc b/ramdisk/etc/init.samsungexynos7420.rc
--- a/ramdisk/etc/init.samsungexynos7420.rc
+++ b/ramdisk/etc/init.samsungexynos7420.rc
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
     restorecon /metadata
 
     # ZRAM setup
-    write /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm lz4
+    write /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm lzo
 
 on init
     start watchdogd
-- 
2.43.0

